id: pm-x4nn3z
title: "The CLI has 195 error codes and contracts none of them: the surface agents read when they are wrong is the only one with no enumeration, no stability promise, and no gate"
description: "Measured 2026-07-26: 195 distinct error codes declared across src, zero present in pm contracts (fourteen keys, none an error catalog) and zero documented in docs. Commands (77) and flags (470 spellings) are both contracted and gated; the third surface is not. Consumers must trigger failures to discover codes, a code can be renamed in a patch with no gate objecting, and 195 codes across 94 files cannot be deduplicated without an enumeration. Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched error-code/taxonomy/contracts/exit-code items across all statuses; pm-185870 unifies one code family, pm-psy1 owns exit-code guarantees, pm-fs8q9x owns flag lexicon. No item enumerates or gates the error vocabulary."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:contracts",diagnostics,error-contract,scripting,simplification
created_at: "2026-07-26T06:02:22.287Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T05:38:49.239Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "pm contracts emits an error-code catalog generated from the same declarations the runtime uses, so it cannot drift; each entry carries code, stable exit code, stable-or-provisional status, emitting commands, and a one-line meaning; a snapshot gate in the shape of contracts:check and sdk:surface:check makes adding a code a reviewed change and makes renaming or removing a stable code fail the build; a deduplication pass applies the one-spelling-per-concept rule from pm-fs8q9x to the 195 codes, merging near-synonyms behind aliases rather than deleting them; a documented code-class to exit-code mapping lets a shell consumer classify a failure from exit status alone, closing the exit-code half of pm-psy1; the catalog is emitted under a surface tier so the default pm contracts payload does not grow"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "The error vocabulary becomes an enumerated, tiered, stability-tagged contract that agents can read before they fail instead of after"
value: Integrations pre-write handlers instead of discovering codes by deliberate failure; a renamed code fails the build instead of breaking consumers silently; the vocabulary becomes reviewable and therefore deduplicable
why_now: "The simplification epic has censused commands and flags twice and never counted error codes; two independent defects in exactly this surface were found in the same review, both of a kind that an enumeration would have exposed on sight"
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: low
confidence: high
