comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T14:27:05.518Z","harness:codex","GitHub report linkage: GH-745 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/745 demonstrates unsupported PmClient actions returning literal 64 while EXIT_CODE.USAGE is 2. Reusing this canonical all-status error-contract feature; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-07-26T14:47:00.511Z","harness:codex","Evidence: SDK native dispatch now imports and uses the canonical EXIT_CODE.USAGE contract for every unsupported extension-action branch. Focused regression tests passed, full coverage passed 374/374 files and 6420/6420 tests at literal 100/100/100/100, lint/static quality/contracts passed, and an unrelated temporary consumer installed the packed tarball and observed exitCode=2 matching the exported EXIT_CODE.USAGE."
  "2026-07-26T15:12:40.567Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/748. Initial exact implementation commit 004790f7; hosted exact-head checks and AI review loop pending."
  "2026-07-26T15:24:34.646Z","harness:codex","Exact-head hosted evidence for PR #748: commit eeb768ba50dde4c902ced790798e93ff43eb0f71 passes the complete GitHub matrix, including Windows regression, macOS/Ubuntu runtime smokes, four coverage shards plus aggregate coverage, static, compatibility, typecheck, package smokes, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, docs, CodeFactor, DeepScan, Hound, Codecov, and Sourcery. The initial Windows-only test-path defect was corrected; the unchanged-head macOS retry passed after GitHub's transient artifact-download ECONNRESET. Thread inventory has no actionable inline feedback. This follow-up intentionally implements the usage exit-code parity escape while the broader catalog remains open."
  "2026-07-29T16:56:42.913Z","harness:claude-code","A misclassification instance for the catalog, build 2026.7.29.\n\nRunning workspace snapshot restore with an empty target produces this envelope: type urn:pm-cli:error:unknown_error, code unknown_error, title \"Unhandled error\", detail \"Snapshot names and fingerprints must use lowercase letters, digits, dots, underscores, or hyphens\", exit_code 1, why \"Unexpected runtime failures can occur from environment or extension-level issues\", examples pm --help and pm health --json.\n\nThe detail is precise and correct - it names a declared input grammar. Everything around it is wrong for the situation: the code says the failure was unexpected, the why blames the environment or an extension, and the recovery examples point at root help and a health check instead of the one command that would supply a valid target, workspace snapshot list.\n\nThe generalisable rule this argues for, alongside the catalog and stability work already in scope here: no violation of a declared input grammar may surface under an unknown or unhandled code. That is checkable as a negative control - feed each documented grammar a deliberately invalid value and assert the emitted code is a typed input error - which makes it a cheap conformance test rather than a review habit.\n"
  "2026-07-30T06:47:43.506Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: a generated SDK error-code catalog now derives from literal runtime declarations, validates ownership/message/remediation metadata, and is guarded against drift by contracts:check."
  "2026-07-30T06:53:18.331Z","harness:codex","Live Sentry linkage: PM-CLI-2Q is the snapshot-name grammar failure already captured in this item’s 2026-07-29 misclassification evidence. The 2026-07-30 14-day Sentry/telemetry release gate is green (critical=0, high=0); retaining the catalog item open until grammar-to-code conformance, deduplication, aliases, and stability semantics are complete."
  "2026-07-30T07:19:00.028Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary: this PR lands the generated 201-code SDK/contracts inventory and drift gate as a reviewable foundation. The canonical feature remains open for runtime-owned meanings/remediation, stable/provisional compatibility rules, alias-preserving deduplication, and grammar-to-code/exit-class conformance."
  "2026-07-30T07:40:07.290Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/822 carries the cohesive SDK/CLI self-describing context-contract bundle. Initial implementation commit e1fabaa97; final exact-head checks and review evidence will be recorded in the PR because post-review tracker mutations would create a new unreviewed Git tree."
  "2026-07-30T07:50:35.989Z","harness:codex","Greptile P1 review correction on PR #822: error exit codes can no longer rely only on vocabulary heuristics. The generator now parses TypeScript syntax, derives explicit PmCliError EXIT_CODE/numeric declarations, fails closed on conflicting declarations, and retains fallback classification only where no executable transport declaration exists."
  "2026-07-30T08:15:45.362Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence for PR #822: error catalog generation now parses TypeScript AST declarations, preserves explicit PmCliError transport exits including EXIT_CODE constants and numeric literals, fails closed on conflicting explicit exits, and uses fallback classification only where no explicit transport exists. Generator coverage is exact 100/100/100/100; full quality, secrets scan, and dependency audit passed with no known vulnerabilities."
  "2026-08-04T19:54:38.932Z","harness:codex","Implementation tranche evidence 2026-08-04: the generated error catalog now exposes semantic exit classes and emitting-command ownership, with an explicit stable/provisional compatibility ledger. Generation fails closed on malformed ledger data, unsupported exits, stable-code removal, and drift; new codes default provisional. Workspace snapshot negative paths now emit typed usage/not-found/conflict classes. All four linked catalog suites passed; direct full coverage is 100/100/100/100 and contracts generation is current. Alias-preserving deduplication and exhaustive grammar-to-code conformance remain open."
  "2026-08-04T20:56:33.386Z","harness:codex","Review evidence: CodeRabbit findings drove fail-closed stability-ledger reads (only ENOENT means absent), write-after-render ordering, unknown_error generic-failure exit 1, cross-cutting '*' emitter retention, and child_process mock parity. Added direct regressions including failed initial generation leaving no ledger, EISDIR propagation, mixed command/cross-cutting sources, and the stable unknown_error mapping. The broader authored per-code meaning/remediation vocabulary remains within this open item's planned runtime-owned metadata scope; this revision preserves the pre-existing generated meaning wording rather than claiming generic text is complete."
  "2026-08-04T20:56:35.007Z","harness:codex","Verification: direct repository coverage passed 433 files / 6850 tests at exactly 100% statements (48776/48776), branches (35358/35358), functions (9975/9975), and lines (47275/47275). Focused generator/output/budget/example suite passed 23/23; linked workspace snapshot CLI integration passed 2/2. Typecheck, ESLint, zero-clone JSCPD, 100% docstring static gate, contracts snapshots, package SDK parity, secrets scan, token/context/retrieval gates, docs/skills, and packed artifact gates passed. Import-cost timing remains locally noisy under load from two unrelated high-CPU Tokenwerk pytest workers and Chrome; no baseline was weakened, and hosted exact-head checks remain authoritative."
  "2026-08-04T21:26:09.300Z","harness:codex","Final outside-diff review correction: definePmErrorCodeCatalog now trims, filters, deduplicates, and sorts sources/emitting_commands before enforcing the non-empty invariant, so whitespace-only declarations fail closed. Regression covers both arrays. Focused test, typecheck, ESLint, contracts check, and direct full coverage passed: 433 files / 6850 tests; 100% statements (48778/48778), branches (35358/35358), functions (9975/9975), lines (47277/47277)."
  "2026-08-04T21:38:52.367Z","harness:codex","Final CodeRabbit correction for PR #895: the SDK catalog resolver regression now asserts class=usage and emitting_commands=[help] in addition to the stable usage exit code. PM-linked catalog tests were normalized from overlapping entries to one canonical generator plus both catalog suites, leaving three distinct gates total. Focused catalog/generator verification passed 2 files and 7 tests; repository typecheck and focused ESLint passed."
  "2026-08-07T05:38:49.239Z","harness:claude-code","Population re-measured 2026-08-07: this item records 195 error codes and the count is now 236.\n\nMeasured by counting distinct code literals across the product source. The growth is authored, not discovered: every new refusal since the item was filed declares a fresh code, which is the correct behaviour and is exactly why the uncontracted population keeps growing. Four of the 236 were added in this session.\n\nThe consumer cost is now demonstrated rather than argued. The release gate that decides whether production errors block a cut classifies them by lowercased message substring, carrying 34 hand-written patterns across four lists and referencing none of the 236 codes, although the handled-error channel already ships the code to that same store as a tag and every refusal envelope carries both the code and a typed error identifier. On 2026-08-07 the scheduled cut failed on one issue whose product behaviour was correct, and the repair had to touch both the product and the prose allowlist. That consumer defect is filed separately and is blocked_by this item, because binding the gate to a code is only safe once the codes are contracted.\n"
